WEBVTT

00:00:00.603 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.778 --> 00:00:03.470
A men's haircut looks simple:

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:04.750
short and neat.

00:00:05.176 --> 00:00:08.350
But precisely because it is short, every mistake shows.

00:00:08.616 --> 00:00:11.710
A dip, a ridge, sideburns that don't match:

00:00:12.036 --> 00:00:14.030
the client sees it in the mirror right away.

00:00:14.379 --> 00:00:18.190
Today, we talk about what makes a men's cut clean and balanced.

00:00:18.717 --> 00:00:21.151
First, let us name the parts of the head.

00:00:21.663 --> 00:00:24.991
On top is the top section, usually kept the longest.

00:00:25.339 --> 00:00:27.151
On each side are the sides.

00:00:27.498 --> 00:00:31.711
At the back is the occipital area, and at the very bottom, the nape.

00:00:32.181 --> 00:00:33.471
Then there is the outline:

00:00:33.813 --> 00:00:36.991
around the ears, the sideburns, and the neckline.

00:00:37.426 --> 00:00:39.871
There are a couple of very important landmarks.

00:00:40.179 --> 00:00:41.391
The parietal ridge:

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:43.951
the widest part of the head, on each side.

00:00:44.202 --> 00:00:48.191
And the occipital bone, the part that sticks out slightly at the back of the head.

00:00:48.696 --> 00:00:52.511
The blend between short and long usually sits around these landmarks.

00:00:53.081 --> 00:00:55.002
Now, clippers and guards.

00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:58.682
A guard is the plastic comb that attaches to the clipper blade.

00:00:59.229 --> 00:01:02.522
The number on the guard tells you roughly how long the hair will be left.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.002
The higher the number, the longer the hair.

00:01:05.428 --> 00:01:07.082
But every brand is a little different:

00:01:07.265 --> 00:01:09.962
the same number can be slightly longer or shorter.

00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:12.762
So check the chart for the brand you are actually using.

00:01:13.233 --> 00:01:15.402
Many clippers also have a lever on the side.

00:01:15.744 --> 00:01:18.464
Move it up or down, and the blade shifts a little,

00:01:18.414 --> 00:01:21.722
so the hair is a touch longer or shorter with the same guard.

00:01:22.076 --> 00:01:25.002
Barbers often use it to blend smoothly between guards.

00:01:25.196 --> 00:01:26.842
And always start with a longer guard.

00:01:27.054 --> 00:01:28.282
You can always cut more.

00:01:28.616 --> 00:01:31.642
Once it is too short, all you can do is wait for it to grow.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.818
Hold the scissors correctly.

00:01:34.074 --> 00:01:38.618
Thumb in one ring, ring finger in the other, little finger resting on the tang.

00:01:39.163 --> 00:01:41.738
When you cut, only the thumb blade moves;

00:01:41.814 --> 00:01:43.338
the other blade stays still.

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:47.258
That keeps the line straight, and the hair is not pushed out of place.

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:51.651
When combing, many stylists take the thumb out and palm the scissors,

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:54.938
so the comb and the scissors don't get in each other's way.

00:01:55.121 --> 00:01:58.218
And never point the tips of the scissors toward the client's face.

00:01:58.861 --> 00:02:01.190
Run the clippers against the direction of growth.

00:02:01.516 --> 00:02:04.550
That lifts the hair, so the blade cuts more evenly.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.974
Keep the guard flat against the head, and move slowly and steadily,

00:02:08.924 --> 00:02:11.110
with each pass overlapping a little.

00:02:11.375 --> 00:02:15.301
At the nape and around whorls, the hair grows in several directions,

00:02:15.251 --> 00:02:18.550
so go over it from a few other directions to even it out.

00:02:18.875 --> 00:02:20.390
A very common mistake:

00:02:20.635 --> 00:02:22.908
pressing the clippers hard into the head,

00:02:22.858 --> 00:02:25.510
or tilting them so the blade digs into the hair.

00:02:25.923 --> 00:02:29.350
That spot ends up shorter than the rest, a hole that really shows.

00:02:29.969 --> 00:02:33.428
To blend the short part into the long part, there are two methods:

00:02:33.673 --> 00:02:36.388
scissor over comb, and clipper over comb.

00:02:36.795 --> 00:02:40.388
The comb sits close to the head, with the teeth angled slightly out.

00:02:40.887 --> 00:02:43.668
Whatever hair sticks out through the teeth, you cut off.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:48.148
The angle of the comb decides whether the hair is left longer or shorter.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:53.108
With scissors, the blade runs parallel to the comb, for a soft blend.

00:02:53.288 --> 00:02:56.948
With the clippers over the comb, it is faster and more even.

00:02:57.375 --> 00:03:01.908
The comb always moves upward, steadily, never staying long in one spot.

00:03:02.239 --> 00:03:03.828
Stop, and you get a step.

00:03:04.385 --> 00:03:08.717
The place where men's cuts most often go wrong is where the sides meet the top.

00:03:09.125 --> 00:03:13.907
The sides are cut short with clippers, the top is left long, and in between,

00:03:13.857 --> 00:03:15.277
there is a hard ridge.

00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:17.757
From the side, it looks like a step.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.603
You have to blend gradually from short to long, with scissor over comb,

00:03:22.553 --> 00:03:24.397
or a longer guard in between,

00:03:24.587 --> 00:03:27.677
until you run your hand up, and no longer see a ridge.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:32.411
What makes a men's cut look professional is balance, and the outline.

00:03:32.987 --> 00:03:36.971
The outline around the ears is neat and natural, not cut too high.

00:03:37.464 --> 00:03:39.291
Both sideburns are the same length.

00:03:39.764 --> 00:03:43.291
The neckline is square or rounded, as the client prefers.

00:03:43.781 --> 00:03:46.095
Uneven sideburns are a very common mistake,

00:03:46.045 --> 00:03:48.411
especially when the client tilts their head.

00:03:48.587 --> 00:03:51.503
Keep the head straight, looking straight into the mirror,

00:03:51.453 --> 00:03:54.571
and place a finger at the bottom of each sideburn to compare.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.891
And do not just look from one side.

00:03:57.159 --> 00:04:00.171
Look in the mirror, from the side, and from behind.

00:04:00.835 --> 00:04:01.767
About hygiene.

00:04:02.429 --> 00:04:05.682
After every client, brush the hair out of the clipper blade,

00:04:05.632 --> 00:04:08.886
disinfect the blade and the guards as the product instructs,

00:04:09.156 --> 00:04:10.087
and oil the blade.

00:04:10.511 --> 00:04:14.647
An oiled blade runs smoothly, stays cooler, and pulls less.

00:04:15.155 --> 00:04:18.647
Combs and scissors are cleaned and disinfected after every client.

00:04:18.917 --> 00:04:20.727
Razor blades are used only once.

00:04:21.023 --> 00:04:24.167
For more detail, watch the lesson on cleaning tools again.

00:04:24.413 --> 00:04:28.172
If the scalp has a wound, inflammation, or lice, don't cut,

00:04:28.122 --> 00:04:31.127
as in the lesson on when not to treat a client.

00:04:31.741 --> 00:04:34.883
Before cutting, you also need to read the client's hair,

00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:37.368
as in the consultation and sectioning lesson.

00:04:37.762 --> 00:04:42.168
Thick, coarse hair cut too short stands straight up, and looks spiky.

00:04:42.435 --> 00:04:45.368
So leave it a little longer, or thin out some of the bulk.

00:04:45.778 --> 00:04:51.368
Thin hair on top left too long falls flat, separates, and shows even more scalp.

00:04:51.795 --> 00:04:53.848
Cutting it shorter often makes it look thicker.

00:04:54.088 --> 00:04:56.648
And look at the whorls at the crown and the nape.

00:04:56.923 --> 00:04:58.168
Don't cut too close there.

00:04:58.811 --> 00:05:00.971
Finally, be honest with the client.

00:05:01.352 --> 00:05:05.899
If the client wants the crown cut really short, and there is a strong whorl there,

00:05:05.849 --> 00:05:07.051
tell them beforehand:

00:05:07.321 --> 00:05:08.571
the hair will stand up.

00:05:09.153 --> 00:05:12.792
If the client brings a photo of someone with thick, coarse hair,

00:05:12.742 --> 00:05:14.811
but their own hair is fine and thin,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:15.931
say clearly:

00:05:16.227 --> 00:05:19.531
we can do that shape, but it won't look exactly like the photo.

00:05:19.869 --> 00:05:23.294
If the client wants a style that needs product every morning,

00:05:23.244 --> 00:05:26.171
but they never use product, suggest an easier style.

00:05:26.431 --> 00:05:30.890
And tell the client that a short cut usually holds its shape for about three to five weeks,

00:05:31.071 --> 00:05:33.291
so they can book the next visit at the right time.

00:05:33.927 --> 00:05:37.471
So you see, a great men's cut is not about speed.

00:05:37.895 --> 00:05:42.030
It is about a soft blend, balanced sides, and a clean outline.

00:05:42.539 --> 00:05:46.271
In the practice lesson, we will cut it step by step, together.

00:05:46.616 --> 00:05:49.551
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:49.723 --> 00:05:50.591
See you next time.
